Description: 3D stills in the clip's properties, and the monitor after a save
 A still (MLT reads JPS, MPO, PNG with sTER and a pair by the photo policy as
 its two views) has the 3D input corrections in its properties, as a video
 clip; its correction is saved into the file by the stereo layer
 (Stereo::Picture::saveCorrection), which writes into JPEG pictures, and a
 picture of another format is refused with that reason. After a save into the
 file the clip is read again and the project monitor shows its frame at once,
 never black until the playhead moves.
